Now the ANSI version of `tty-clock.c`.

I'll use `\e[H` (home), `\e[J` (clear), `\e[row;colH` (move), `\e[m` (color).
Colors: `\e[3Xm` for foreground, `\e[4Xm` for background.
ACS: `\x0e` starts ACS, `\x0f` ends ACS (for some terminals), or `\e(0` / `\e(B`.
Actually, looking at my tmux capture:
`lqqqqqqqk`
`` is `0x0e`, `` is `0x0f`. These are SO (Shift Out) and SI (Shift In) characters.

```c
