static int running = 1;

void cleanup(void) {
    tcsetattr(STDIN_FILENO, TCSANOW, &TtyClock.oldterm);
    printf("\e[?25h\e[0m"); // Show cursor, reset colors
}

void sig_handler(int sig) {
    if (sig == SIGINT || sig == SIGTERM) running = 0;
    if (sig == SIGWINCH) {
        struct winsize w;
        ioctl(STDOUT_FILENO, TIOCGWINSZ, &w);
        TtyClock.term_w = w.ws_col;
        TtyClock.term_h = w.ws_row;
    }
}

// ... rest of the code ...
```

Wait, `select()` for non-blocking input with timeout is good.
The delay is `delay` seconds + `nsdelay` nanoseconds.

```c
struct timeval tv;
tv.tv_sec = TtyClock.delay;
tv.tv_usec = TtyClock.nsdelay / 1000;
```

Actually, `nanosleep` is better for precision, and I can use `poll()` or `select()` for input with a small timeout.

Wait, I need to implement `draw_digit`, `draw_colon`, and `draw_clock` using `printf`.

```c
void move_cursor(int x, int y) {
